<title>USA: Pharmacia CEO departure has bright side - NYT.</title>
<headline>Pharmacia CEO departure has bright side - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Some analysts see a bright side to the recent surprise resignation of Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn chief executive John Zabriskie, the New York Times said on Thursday in its Market Place column.</p>
<p>It said analysts believe Zabriskie's departure makes little immediate difference on the company's operations.</p>
<p>It said one analyst with a health care investing firm projected three years of annual earnings growth of 17 to 18 percent for the company. An analyst with Salomon Brothers said the stock price would remain in the high 30s for the next three to six months, it said.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
</text>
